WEBVTT

00:00:03.994 --> 00:00:05.427
Sammy!

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:07.327
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can!

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:08.427
Go!

00:00:11.161 --> 00:00:13.360
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:13.393 --> 00:00:15.161
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:17.994 --> 00:00:20.293
This is dad's book.

00:00:20.327 --> 00:00:22.161
I think he wants us to
pick up where he left off -

00:00:22.194 --> 00:00:25.861
Saving people, hunting
things, the family business.

00:00:25.894 --> 00:00:28.927
I got to find dad. It's the
only think i can think about.

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:36.094
Bethany: now i lay me down to sleep.

00:00:36.128 --> 00:00:38.293
I pray the lord my soul to keep.

00:00:38.327 --> 00:00:41.027
Thy angels watch me through the night

00:00:41.061 --> 00:00:43.794
And keep me safe till morning light.

00:00:43.827 --> 00:00:46.761
Amen.

00:00:54.460 --> 00:00:57.260
Night, monkeypuss.

00:00:57.293 --> 00:00:59.094
Daddy?

00:00:59.128 --> 00:01:01.161
Is mommy coming home?

00:01:04.761 --> 00:01:07.027
No, honey.

00:01:07.061 --> 00:01:10.128
She's spending the night at
the hospital with your sister.

00:01:10.161 --> 00:01:11.460
Hey.

00:01:11.494 --> 00:01:13.627
You sleep tight now.

00:03:07.977 --> 00:03:11.177
Dean: yeah, you probably
missed something.

00:03:11.210 --> 00:03:13.344
Dude, i ran lexisnexis,
local police reports,

00:03:13.377 --> 00:03:15.644
Newspapers
- I couldn't find a single red flag.

00:03:15.677 --> 00:03:17.744
Are you sure you got
the coordinates right?

00:03:17.778 --> 00:03:18.878
Yeah, i double-Checked.

00:03:18.910 --> 00:03:20.210
It's fitchburg, wisconsin.

00:03:20.244 --> 00:03:22.210
Dad wouldn't have sent us coordinates

00:03:22.244 --> 00:03:23.878
If it wasn't important, sammy.

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:25.210
Well, i'm telling you, i looked,

00:03:25.244 --> 00:03:27.244
And all i could find was a
big, steamy pile of nothing.

00:03:27.277 --> 00:03:28.577
If dad's sending us
hunting for something,

00:03:28.611 --> 00:03:29.644
I don't know what.

00:03:29.677 --> 00:03:31.144
Well, maybe he's gonna meet us there.

00:03:31.177 --> 00:03:34.344
Yeah, 'cause he's been so
easy to find up to this point.

00:03:34.377 --> 00:03:36.544
You're a real smartass, you know that?

00:03:36.577 --> 00:03:37.910
Don't worry.

00:03:37.943 --> 00:03:40.310
I'm sure there's something
in fitchburg worth killing.

00:03:40.344 --> 00:03:42.544
Yeah? What makes you so sure?

00:03:42.577 --> 00:03:45.744
Because i'm the oldest,
which means i'm always right.

00:03:45.778 --> 00:03:48.477
No, it doesn't. It totally does.

00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:06.611
Well, the waitress thinks

00:04:06.644 --> 00:04:09.778
That the local freemasons
are up to something sneaky,

00:04:09.811 --> 00:04:11.077
But other than that,

00:04:11.110 --> 00:04:13.844
Nobody's heard about
anything weird going on.

00:04:13.878 --> 00:04:17.277
Dean, you got the time?

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:19.577
10 after 4:00.

00:04:19.611 --> 00:04:21.177
Why?

00:04:21.210 --> 00:04:24.344
What's wrong with this picture?

00:04:29.444 --> 00:04:32.677
School's out, isn't it?

00:04:32.711 --> 00:04:34.310
Yeah.

00:04:37.144 --> 00:04:38.811
So where is everybody?

00:04:38.844 --> 00:04:42.577
This place should be
crawling with kids right now.

00:04:56.344 --> 00:04:58.977
It sure is quiet out here.

00:04:59.010 --> 00:05:00.778
Yeah, it's a shame.

00:05:00.811 --> 00:05:02.077
Why is that?

00:05:02.110 --> 00:05:05.577
You know, kids getting
sick. It's a terrible thing.

00:05:05.611 --> 00:05:07.910
How many?

00:05:07.943 --> 00:05:12.444
Just five or six, but
serious, hospital serious.

00:05:12.477 --> 00:05:15.177
A lot of parents are
getting pretty anxious.

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:16.744
They think it's catching.

00:05:30.477 --> 00:05:32.844
Dude, dude, i am not using this i.D.

00:05:32.878 --> 00:05:34.010
Why not?

00:05:34.043 --> 00:05:36.077
Because it says "bikini
inspector" on it.

00:05:36.110 --> 00:05:38.043
Don't worry. She won't look that close.

00:05:38.077 --> 00:05:39.844
Hell, she won't even ask to see it.

00:05:39.878 --> 00:05:41.210
It's all about confidence, sammy.

00:05:42.344 --> 00:05:44.144
Hi.

00:05:44.177 --> 00:05:47.110
I'm dr. Jerry kaplan,
center for disease control.

00:05:47.144 --> 00:05:49.244
Can i see some i.D.?

00:05:52.177 --> 00:05:54.411
Yeah, of course.

00:05:56.744 --> 00:05:59.644
Now, could you direct me
to the pediatrics ward?

00:05:59.677 --> 00:06:03.144
Okay, just go down that hall,
turn left, up the stairs.

00:06:03.177 --> 00:06:04.644
You'll see them.

00:06:04.677 --> 00:06:06.477
Right. Thank you.

00:06:06.511 --> 00:06:08.611
See? Told you it would work.

00:06:08.644 --> 00:06:11.411
Follow me. It's upstairs.

00:06:45.677 --> 00:06:47.010
Sam: dean.

00:06:56.344 --> 00:06:58.377
Thanks for seeing us, dr. Hydaker.

00:06:58.411 --> 00:07:00.277
Oh, i'm glad you guys are here.

00:07:00.310 --> 00:07:02.677
I was just about to call the cdc myself.

00:07:02.711 --> 00:07:04.444
How did you find out anyway?

00:07:04.477 --> 00:07:06.644
Oh, some g.P. - I
forget his name -

00:07:06.677 --> 00:07:09.677
He called atlanta and must
have beat you to the punch.

00:07:09.711 --> 00:07:12.477
So you say you got six cases so far?

00:07:12.511 --> 00:07:14.878
Yeah, in five weeks.

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:17.411
At first i thought it
was bacterial pneumonia,

00:07:17.444 --> 00:07:18.544
Not that newsworthy.

00:07:18.577 --> 00:07:20.444
But now...

00:07:20.477 --> 00:07:22.611
Now, what?

00:07:22.644 --> 00:07:24.977
The kids aren't
responding to antibiotics.

00:07:25.010 --> 00:07:27.277
Their white-Cell
counts keep going down.

00:07:27.310 --> 00:07:30.010
Their immune systems just
aren't doing their job.

00:07:30.043 --> 00:07:32.844
It's like their bodies are wearing out.

00:07:32.878 --> 00:07:34.444
Betty: excuse me, dr. Hydaker.

00:07:34.477 --> 00:07:36.244
You ever see anything like this before?

00:07:36.277 --> 00:07:37.411
Never this severe.

00:07:37.444 --> 00:07:39.943
The way it spreads
- That's a new one for me.

00:07:39.977 --> 00:07:41.210
What do you mean?

00:07:41.244 --> 00:07:42.744
It works its way through families,

00:07:42.778 --> 00:07:45.977
But only the children,
one sibling after another.

00:07:46.010 --> 00:07:49.477
You mind if we interview
a few of the kids?

00:07:49.511 --> 00:07:51.644
They're not conscious.

00:07:51.677 --> 00:07:53.811
None of them?

00:07:53.844 --> 00:07:55.644
No.

00:07:55.677 --> 00:07:58.844
Can we talk to the parents?

00:08:00.277 --> 00:08:02.210
If you think it'll help.

00:08:02.244 --> 00:08:05.811
Yeah, yeah. Who was your
most recent admission?

00:08:05.844 --> 00:08:08.077
I should get back to my girls.

00:08:08.110 --> 00:08:09.344
We understand that,

00:08:09.377 --> 00:08:12.077
And we really appreciate
you talking to us.

00:08:12.110 --> 00:08:14.144
Now, you say mary's the oldest?

00:08:14.177 --> 00:08:15.377
13.

00:08:15.411 --> 00:08:17.577
Okay, and she came down
with it first, right?

00:08:17.611 --> 00:08:18.677
And then...

00:08:18.711 --> 00:08:20.844
Bethany the next night.

00:08:20.878 --> 00:08:22.744
Within 24 hours?

00:08:22.778 --> 00:08:25.511
I guess.

00:08:25.544 --> 00:08:28.611
Look, i already went through
all this with the doctor.

00:08:28.644 --> 00:08:30.644
Right. Just a few more
questions, if you don't mind.

00:08:30.677 --> 00:08:32.577
How do you think they caught pneumonia?

00:08:32.611 --> 00:08:34.778
Were they out in the
cold, anything like that?

00:08:34.811 --> 00:08:36.943
No, we think it was an open window.

00:08:36.977 --> 00:08:39.277
Both times?

00:08:39.310 --> 00:08:42.878
The first time, i don't really remember,

00:08:42.910 --> 00:08:44.444
But the second time for sure,

00:08:44.477 --> 00:08:47.477
And i know i closed it
before i put bethany to bed.

00:08:47.511 --> 00:08:49.010
So you think she opened it?

00:08:49.043 --> 00:08:51.577
It's a second-Story window, no ledge.

00:08:51.611 --> 00:08:53.177
No one else could have.

00:08:57.744 --> 00:09:00.310
You know this might not
be anything supernatural.

00:09:00.344 --> 00:09:01.943
It might just be pneumonia.

00:09:01.977 --> 00:09:04.210
Maybe. Or maybe something
opened that window.

00:09:04.244 --> 00:09:07.110
I don't know, man. Look, dad
sent us down here for a reason.

00:09:07.144 --> 00:09:09.444
I think we might be
barking up the right tree.

00:09:09.477 --> 00:09:10.544
I'll tell you one thing.

00:09:10.577 --> 00:09:11.544
What?

00:09:11.577 --> 00:09:13.310
That guy we just talked to -

00:09:13.344 --> 00:09:16.110
I'm betting it'll be a
while before he goes home.

00:09:25.744 --> 00:09:28.177
You got anything over there?

00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:29.878
No, nothing.

00:09:29.910 --> 00:09:33.244
Yeah, me neither.

00:09:43.878 --> 00:09:45.344
Hey, dean.

00:09:45.377 --> 00:09:47.110
Dean: yeah?

00:09:48.611 --> 00:09:53.377
You were right. It's not pneumonia.

00:09:57.144 --> 00:09:59.310
It's rotted.

00:10:03.244 --> 00:10:05.844
What the hell leaves
a handprint like that?

00:10:09.177 --> 00:10:10.910
<i>Man: cheetara.</i>

00:10:10.943 --> 00:10:12.110
<i>Woman: i am sorry to wake you,</i>

00:10:12.144 --> 00:10:13.544
<i>But jaga bids me to bring you to him.</i>

00:10:13.577 --> 00:10:15.577
John: all right.

00:10:16.611 --> 00:10:18.177
You know the drill, dean.

00:10:18.210 --> 00:10:20.511
If anyone calls, you don't pick up.

00:10:20.544 --> 00:10:23.878
If it's me, i'll ring
once and then call back.

00:10:23.910 --> 00:10:25.244
You got that?

00:10:25.277 --> 00:10:28.577
Mm-Hmm. Don't answer the phone
unless it rings once first.

00:10:28.611 --> 00:10:31.210
Come on, dude. Look alive.
This stuff's important.

00:10:31.244 --> 00:10:32.344
I know, it's just,

00:10:32.377 --> 00:10:34.811
We've done it like a million times,

00:10:34.844 --> 00:10:36.644
And you know i'm not stupid.

00:10:36.677 --> 00:10:38.811
I know you're not, but
it only takes one mistake.

00:10:38.844 --> 00:10:40.210
You got that?

00:10:40.244 --> 00:10:43.611
<i>It's important that he join
jaga on the flight deck.</i>

00:10:43.644 --> 00:10:46.210
All right, if i'm not
back sunday night...

00:10:46.244 --> 00:10:47.611
Call pastor jim.

00:10:49.943 --> 00:10:52.511
Lock the doors and
windows, close the shades,

00:10:52.544 --> 00:10:53.744
And most important -

00:10:53.778 --> 00:10:55.310
Watch out for sammy.

00:10:55.344 --> 00:10:57.677
<i>Responsible for lion-O's
welfare, snarf is.</i>

00:10:57.711 --> 00:10:58.943
I know.

00:10:58.977 --> 00:11:00.611
All right, if something
tries to bust in...

00:11:00.644 --> 00:11:03.611
Shoot first, ask questions later.

00:11:03.644 --> 00:11:05.744
That's my man.

00:11:09.711 --> 00:11:11.010
<i>What's up, jaga?</i>

00:11:11.043 --> 00:11:12.110
<i>Come closer.</i>

00:11:16.943 --> 00:11:19.611
<i>What's happening to her?</i>

00:11:21.544 --> 00:11:23.411
<i>What was that?</i>

00:11:23.444 --> 00:11:26.010
Dean: i know why dad sent us here.

00:11:30.744 --> 00:11:32.844
He's faced this thing before.

00:11:34.910 --> 00:11:38.778
He wants us to finish the job.

00:12:01.183 --> 00:12:02.884
So what the hell is a shtriga?

00:12:02.917 --> 00:12:04.817
It's kind of like a witch, i think.

00:12:04.851 --> 00:12:06.484
I don't know much about them.

00:12:06.517 --> 00:12:08.484
Well, i've never heard of it,

00:12:08.517 --> 00:12:10.517
And it's not in dad's journal.

00:12:10.550 --> 00:12:13.183
Dad hunted one in fort
douglas, wisconsin,

00:12:13.217 --> 00:12:14.651
About 16, 17 years ago.

00:12:14.684 --> 00:12:17.517
You were there. You don't remember? No.

00:12:17.550 --> 00:12:20.018
I guess he caught wind that
the thing's in fitchburg now

00:12:20.051 --> 00:12:21.517
And kicked us the coordinates.

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:23.784
So wait, this... shtriga.

00:12:23.817 --> 00:12:25.751
Right, you think it's the
same one dad hunted before?

00:12:25.784 --> 00:12:28.283
Yeah, maybe.

00:12:28.317 --> 00:12:30.317
If dad went after it, why
is it still breathing air?

00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:31.484
Because it got away.

00:12:31.517 --> 00:12:32.617
Got away?

00:12:32.651 --> 00:12:34.018
Yeah, sammy, it happens.

00:12:34.051 --> 00:12:35.217
Not very often.

00:12:35.250 --> 00:12:36.517
I don't know what to tell you.

00:12:36.550 --> 00:12:38.384
Maybe dad didn't have
his wheaties that morning.

00:12:38.417 --> 00:12:40.217
What else do you remember?

00:12:40.250 --> 00:12:42.450
Nothing. I was a kid, all right?

00:12:52.217 --> 00:12:53.851
King or two queens?

00:12:53.884 --> 00:12:55.450
Two queens.

00:12:59.550 --> 00:13:01.118
Yeah, i bet.

00:13:01.150 --> 00:13:02.317
What'd you say?

00:13:02.350 --> 00:13:04.283
Nice car.

00:13:04.317 --> 00:13:06.450
Hi. Checking in?

00:13:06.484 --> 00:13:07.684
Yeah.

00:13:07.717 --> 00:13:11.250
Uh, do me a favor. Go get
your brother some dinner.

00:13:11.283 --> 00:13:13.051
I'm helping a guest.

00:13:16.684 --> 00:13:18.851
Two queens.

00:13:20.984 --> 00:13:22.283
Funny kid.

00:13:22.317 --> 00:13:24.150
Oh, yeah, he thinks so.

00:13:24.183 --> 00:13:25.917
Will that be cash or credit?

00:13:25.951 --> 00:13:27.550
Do you take mastercard? Mm-Hmm.

00:13:27.584 --> 00:13:28.584
Perfect.

00:13:28.617 --> 00:13:29.684
There you go.

00:13:29.717 --> 00:13:32.118
Thank you.

00:13:47.984 --> 00:13:50.584
When's dad gonna get back?

00:13:50.617 --> 00:13:52.118
Tomorrow.

00:13:52.150 --> 00:13:53.350
When?

00:13:53.384 --> 00:13:54.384
I don't know.

00:13:54.417 --> 00:13:56.250
He usually comes in late, though.

00:13:56.283 --> 00:13:58.018
Now, eat your dinner.

00:13:58.051 --> 00:14:00.283
I'm sick of "scabetti-Os."

00:14:00.317 --> 00:14:02.917
Well, you're the one who wanted them.

00:14:02.951 --> 00:14:04.350
I want lucky charms.

00:14:04.384 --> 00:14:05.951
There's no more lucky charms.

00:14:05.984 --> 00:14:07.250
I saw the box.

00:14:07.283 --> 00:14:08.550
Okay, maybe there is,

00:14:08.584 --> 00:14:11.150
But there's only enough
left for one bowl,

00:14:11.183 --> 00:14:12.751
And i haven't had any yet.

00:14:36.517 --> 00:14:38.951
Do you want the prize?

00:14:38.984 --> 00:14:41.384
Sir?

00:14:43.183 --> 00:14:45.217
Thanks.

00:14:55.851 --> 00:14:57.517
Well, you were right.

00:14:57.550 --> 00:15:01.283
It wasn't very easy to
find, but you were right.

00:15:01.317 --> 00:15:03.784
A shtriga is a kind of witch.

00:15:03.817 --> 00:15:05.051
They're albanian,

00:15:05.084 --> 00:15:08.018
But legends about them
date back to ancient rome.

00:15:08.051 --> 00:15:10.118
They feed off of spiritus vitae.

00:15:10.150 --> 00:15:11.784
Spirit what?

00:15:11.817 --> 00:15:13.084
Vitae. It's latin.

00:15:13.118 --> 00:15:15.183
It translates to "breath of life,"

00:15:15.217 --> 00:15:18.517
Kind of like your life force or essence.

00:15:18.550 --> 00:15:20.517
Didn't the doctor say the
kids' bodies were wearing out?

00:15:20.550 --> 00:15:22.484
It's a thought.

00:15:22.517 --> 00:15:23.951
You know, she takes your vitality,

00:15:23.984 --> 00:15:26.118
Maybe your immunity goes to
hell, pneumonia takes hold.

00:15:26.150 --> 00:15:29.350
Anyway, shtrigas can feed
off anyone, but they prefer -

00:15:29.384 --> 00:15:31.118
Children.

00:15:31.150 --> 00:15:32.384
Yeah.

00:15:32.417 --> 00:15:34.484
Probably because they
have stronger life force.

00:15:34.517 --> 00:15:38.118
And get this
- Shtrigas are invulnerable

00:15:38.150 --> 00:15:40.717
To all weapons devised by god and man.

00:15:40.751 --> 00:15:42.951
No, that's not right.

00:15:42.984 --> 00:15:46.450
She's vulnerable when she feeds.

00:15:46.484 --> 00:15:47.484
What?

00:15:47.517 --> 00:15:49.450
If you catch her when she's eating,

00:15:49.484 --> 00:15:52.018
You can blast her with
consecrated wrought irons,

00:15:52.051 --> 00:15:53.884
Buckshots or rounds i think.

00:15:53.917 --> 00:15:55.550
How do you know that?

00:15:55.584 --> 00:15:58.384
Dad told me. I remember.

00:15:58.417 --> 00:16:00.817
Oh.

00:16:00.851 --> 00:16:04.884
So, uh, anything else
dad might have mentioned?

00:16:04.917 --> 00:16:07.217
No, that's it.

00:16:09.283 --> 00:16:11.384
What?

00:16:13.450 --> 00:16:15.417
Nothing.

00:16:15.450 --> 00:16:19.250
Okay, so, assuming we
can kill it when it eats,

00:16:19.283 --> 00:16:21.084
We've still got to find the thing first,

00:16:21.118 --> 00:16:22.617
Which ain't gonna be a cakewalk.

00:16:22.651 --> 00:16:25.051
Shtrigas take on a human
disguise when they're not hunting.

00:16:25.084 --> 00:16:26.751
What kind of human disguise?

00:16:26.784 --> 00:16:28.584
Historically, something innocuous.

00:16:28.617 --> 00:16:31.417
It could be anything, but it's
usually a feeble old woman,

00:16:31.450 --> 00:16:34.450
Which may be how the witches-As-
Old-Crones legend got started.

00:16:34.484 --> 00:16:35.550
Hang on.

00:16:35.584 --> 00:16:36.651
What?

00:16:38.651 --> 00:16:39.884
Check this out.

00:16:39.917 --> 00:16:42.084
I marked down all the
addresses of the victims.

00:16:42.118 --> 00:16:44.118
Now, these are the houses
that have been hit so far,

00:16:44.150 --> 00:16:45.350
And dead center -

00:16:45.384 --> 00:16:47.584
The hospital.

00:16:47.617 --> 00:16:50.751
When we were there, i saw
a patient, an old woman.

00:16:50.784 --> 00:16:52.183
An old person, huh?

00:16:52.217 --> 00:16:53.250
Yeah.

00:16:53.283 --> 00:16:54.350
In the hospital?

00:16:54.384 --> 00:16:56.417
Whew! Better call the coast guard.

00:16:56.450 --> 00:16:57.751
Well, listen, smartass,

00:16:57.784 --> 00:17:00.417
She had an inverted
cross hanging on her wall.

00:17:15.484 --> 00:17:17.651
Betty: good night, dr. Hydaker.

00:17:17.684 --> 00:17:19.217
See you tomorrow, betty.

00:17:19.250 --> 00:17:21.350
Try to get some sleep, aaron.

00:17:27.384 --> 00:17:28.784
Come on.

00:18:30.183 --> 00:18:32.384
Who the hell are you?

00:18:32.417 --> 00:18:33.684
Who's there?

00:18:35.817 --> 00:18:37.951
You trying to steal my stuff?

00:18:37.984 --> 00:18:39.851
They're always stealing around here.

00:18:39.884 --> 00:18:42.684
No, ma'am, we're
maintenance. We're sorry.

00:18:42.717 --> 00:18:44.317
We thought you were sleeping.

00:18:44.350 --> 00:18:46.051
Ah, nonsense.

00:18:46.084 --> 00:18:48.384
I was sleeping with my peepers open.

00:18:51.851 --> 00:18:54.817
And fix that crucifix, would you?

00:18:54.851 --> 00:18:58.317
I've asked four damn times already.

00:19:55.707 --> 00:19:59.007
"I was sleeping with my peepers open."

00:19:59.041 --> 00:20:02.341
I almost smoked that old gal, i swear.

00:20:02.374 --> 00:20:03.774
It's not funny.

00:20:04.801 --> 00:20:07.034
Oh, man, you should have
seen your face, dean.

00:20:07.067 --> 00:20:09.667
Oh, yeah, laugh it on, man.
We're back to square one.

00:20:12.234 --> 00:20:14.933
Hang on.

00:20:23.567 --> 00:20:26.200
Hey, what's wrong?

00:20:26.234 --> 00:20:29.134
My brother's sick.

00:20:29.167 --> 00:20:30.301
The little guy?

00:20:30.334 --> 00:20:32.200
Pneumonia.

00:20:32.234 --> 00:20:34.668
He's in the hospital.

00:20:36.067 --> 00:20:37.800
It's my fault.

00:20:37.833 --> 00:20:39.501
No, come on. How?

00:20:40.668 --> 00:20:43.267
I should have made sure
the window was latched.

00:20:43.301 --> 00:20:45.501
He wouldn't have gotten pneumonia

00:20:45.534 --> 00:20:47.167
If the window was latched.

00:20:51.000 --> 00:20:53.167
Listen to me.

00:20:53.200 --> 00:20:57.634
I can promise you that this
is not your fault, okay?

00:20:57.668 --> 00:21:00.100
It's my job to look after him.

00:21:06.933 --> 00:21:08.334
Michael.

00:21:10.768 --> 00:21:13.334
Turn on the "no vacancy"
sign while i'm gone.

00:21:13.367 --> 00:21:15.100
I've got denise covering room service,

00:21:15.134 --> 00:21:16.200
So don't bother with the rooms.

00:21:16.234 --> 00:21:17.567
I'm going with you. Not now, michael.

00:21:17.601 --> 00:21:18.701
But i got to see asher.

00:21:18.734 --> 00:21:20.167
Dean: hey, michael.

00:21:20.200 --> 00:21:21.534
Hey.

00:21:21.567 --> 00:21:24.334
I know how you feel.
I'm a big brother, too.

00:21:24.367 --> 00:21:27.067
But you got to go easy on
your mom right now, okay?

00:21:27.100 --> 00:21:28.267
Aw, damn it.

00:21:28.301 --> 00:21:29.567
I got it.

00:21:29.601 --> 00:21:32.334
Thanks. You're in no condition to drive.

00:21:32.367 --> 00:21:35.100
Why don't you let me give
you a lift to the hospital?

00:21:35.134 --> 00:21:36.434
No, no, i couldn't possibly -

00:21:36.467 --> 00:21:40.067
No, no trouble. I insist.

00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:48.000
Be good.

00:21:54.668 --> 00:21:56.401
We're gonna kill this thing.

00:21:56.434 --> 00:21:58.501
I want it dead. You hear me?

00:22:17.100 --> 00:22:18.134
Dean: hey.

00:22:18.167 --> 00:22:19.567
Hey, how's the kid?

00:22:19.601 --> 00:22:22.034
He's not good. Where you at?

00:22:22.067 --> 00:22:23.601
I'm at the library,

00:22:23.634 --> 00:22:26.167
Trying to find out as much
as i can about this shtriga.

00:22:26.200 --> 00:22:27.833
Yeah, what do you got?

00:22:27.867 --> 00:22:29.067
Well, bad news.

00:22:29.100 --> 00:22:31.301
I started with fort douglas

00:22:31.334 --> 00:22:33.501
Around the time you said dad was there.

00:22:33.534 --> 00:22:34.768
And?

00:22:34.800 --> 00:22:35.933
Same deal.

00:22:35.967 --> 00:22:39.334
Before that, there was ogdenville.

00:22:39.367 --> 00:22:43.234
Before that, north
haverbrook and brockway.

00:22:43.267 --> 00:22:46.967
Every 15 to 20 years,
it hits a new town.

00:22:47.000 --> 00:22:50.434
Dean, this thing is just
getting started in fitchburg.

00:22:50.467 --> 00:22:53.367
In all these other places,
it goes on for months,

00:22:53.401 --> 00:22:56.501
Dozens of kids, before the
shtriga finally moves on.

00:22:56.534 --> 00:23:00.100
Kids just languish in
comas, and then they die.

00:23:00.134 --> 00:23:02.301
How far back does this thing go?

00:23:02.334 --> 00:23:03.467
I don't know.

00:23:03.501 --> 00:23:06.167
The earliest mention i
could find is this place

00:23:06.200 --> 00:23:08.668
Called black river
falls back in the 1890s.

00:23:08.701 --> 00:23:11.501
Talk about a horror show.

00:23:13.234 --> 00:23:15.501
Whoa.

00:23:15.534 --> 00:23:16.534
Sam?

00:23:16.567 --> 00:23:18.000
Hold on.

00:23:18.034 --> 00:23:20.367
I'm looking at a photograph right now

00:23:20.401 --> 00:23:23.601
Of a bunch of doctors
standing around a kid's bed.

00:23:23.634 --> 00:23:26.501
One of the doctors is hydaker.

00:23:26.534 --> 00:23:28.067
And?

00:23:28.100 --> 00:23:31.334
And this picture was taken in 1893.

00:23:31.367 --> 00:23:33.534
You sure?

00:23:33.567 --> 00:23:35.134
Yeah.

00:23:35.167 --> 00:23:37.634
Yeah, absolutely.

00:23:56.134 --> 00:24:00.334
Don't worry. Your son's in good hands.

00:24:00.367 --> 00:24:03.601
I'm gonna take care of him.

00:24:03.634 --> 00:24:06.567
So what's the cdc come up with so far?

00:24:06.601 --> 00:24:09.100
We're still working on a few theories.

00:24:09.134 --> 00:24:11.701
You'll know something as soon as we do.

00:24:11.734 --> 00:24:15.167
Well, nothing's more important
to me than these kids.

00:24:15.200 --> 00:24:16.167
Hmm.

00:24:16.200 --> 00:24:18.534
Just let me know if i can help.

00:24:18.567 --> 00:24:21.768
I'll do that.

00:24:24.100 --> 00:24:26.534
Sam: we should have
thought of this before.

00:24:26.567 --> 00:24:29.000
Doctor's a perfect
disguise. You're trusted.

00:24:29.034 --> 00:24:30.900
You can control the whole thing.

00:24:30.933 --> 00:24:34.933
Huh. That son of a bitch.

00:24:34.967 --> 00:24:37.000
I'm surprised you didn't
draw on him right there.

00:24:37.034 --> 00:24:40.000
Yeah, well...

00:24:40.034 --> 00:24:42.000
First of all,

00:24:42.034 --> 00:24:43.967
I'm not gonna open fire in
a freakin' pediatrics ward.

00:24:44.000 --> 00:24:45.668
Good call.

00:24:45.701 --> 00:24:47.267
Second, it wouldn't have done any good

00:24:47.301 --> 00:24:48.668
Because the bastard's bulletproof

00:24:48.701 --> 00:24:50.267
Unless he's chowing down on something.

00:24:50.301 --> 00:24:51.501
And third, i wasn't packing,

00:24:51.534 --> 00:24:53.067
Which is probably a really good thing

00:24:53.100 --> 00:24:55.200
'Cause i probably would have
just burned a clip in him

00:24:55.234 --> 00:24:56.634
Off of principle alone.

00:24:56.668 --> 00:24:59.234
You're getting wise
in your old age, dean.

00:24:59.267 --> 00:25:00.467
You're damn right.

00:25:00.501 --> 00:25:03.100
'Cause now i know how
we're gonna get it.

00:25:03.134 --> 00:25:05.134
What do you mean?

00:25:05.167 --> 00:25:07.000
The shtriga
- It works through siblings, right?

00:25:07.034 --> 00:25:08.134
Right.

00:25:08.167 --> 00:25:09.534
Well, last night...

00:25:09.567 --> 00:25:10.768
It went after asher.

00:25:10.800 --> 00:25:12.701
Tonight it's probably
gonna come after michael.

00:25:12.734 --> 00:25:13.867
Then we got to get him out of here.

00:25:13.900 --> 00:25:16.167
No. No, that would blow the whole deal.

00:25:16.200 --> 00:25:17.668
What? Yeah.

00:25:17.701 --> 00:25:20.100
Then you want to use the kid as bait?

00:25:21.167 --> 00:25:23.933
Are you nuts? No. Forget it.
That's out of the question.

00:25:23.967 --> 00:25:26.467
Sam, it's the only way
- If this thing disappears,

00:25:26.501 --> 00:25:28.800
It could be years before
we get another chance.

00:25:28.833 --> 00:25:30.567
Michael's a kid, and
i'm not gonna dangle him

00:25:30.601 --> 00:25:32.334
In front of that thing
like a worm on a hook.

00:25:32.367 --> 00:25:34.334
Dad did not send me here to walk away.

00:25:34.367 --> 00:25:36.534
<i>Send you here? He didn't send you here.</i>

00:25:36.567 --> 00:25:38.768
<i>He sent us here. This
isn't about you, sam.</i>

00:25:38.800 --> 00:25:40.601
I'm the one that screwed
up. It's my fault.

00:25:40.634 --> 00:25:42.701
There's no telling how
many kids have gotten hurt

00:25:42.734 --> 00:25:43.833
Because of me.

00:25:43.867 --> 00:25:47.434
What are you saying,
dean? How is it your fault?

00:25:53.234 --> 00:25:54.668
Dean.

00:25:54.701 --> 00:25:57.933
You've been hiding
something from the get-Go.

00:25:57.967 --> 00:26:00.601
Since when does dad bail on a hunt?

00:26:00.634 --> 00:26:03.668
Since when does he
let something get away?

00:26:03.701 --> 00:26:08.900
Now, talk to me, man.
Tell me what's going on.

00:26:18.467 --> 00:26:21.234
Fort douglas, wisconsin.

00:26:21.267 --> 00:26:24.267
It was the third night
in this crap room,

00:26:24.301 --> 00:26:26.900
And i was climbing the walls, man.

00:26:26.933 --> 00:26:28.734
I needed to get some air.

00:26:28.768 --> 00:26:30.367
<i>...if ever i saw one.</i>

00:26:30.401 --> 00:26:32.000
<i>Command performance.</i>

00:26:58.933 --> 00:27:00.267
Hey, kid.

00:27:01.434 --> 00:27:03.434
We're closing up.

00:28:06.833 --> 00:28:08.134
Get out of the way!

00:28:18.467 --> 00:28:22.701
Sammy. Sammy. Sammy.

00:28:22.734 --> 00:28:24.000
You okay?

00:28:24.034 --> 00:28:26.768
Sam: dad, what's going on?

00:28:26.800 --> 00:28:28.634
Are you all right?

00:28:32.234 --> 00:28:35.634
What happened?

00:28:35.668 --> 00:28:37.701
I
- I just went out.

00:28:37.734 --> 00:28:39.401
What?

00:28:39.434 --> 00:28:42.067
J
- Just for a second. I'm sorry.

00:28:42.100 --> 00:28:44.467
I told you not to leave this room.

00:28:44.501 --> 00:28:47.467
I told you not to let
him out of your sight.

00:28:59.668 --> 00:29:03.933
Dad just grabbed us and booked,

00:29:03.967 --> 00:29:09.501
Dropped us off at pastor
jim's about three hours away.

00:29:09.534 --> 00:29:12.301
By the time he got back to fort douglas,

00:29:12.334 --> 00:29:14.200
The shtriga had disappeared.

00:29:14.234 --> 00:29:16.467
It was just gone.

00:29:19.501 --> 00:29:23.668
It never resurfaced until now.

00:29:23.701 --> 00:29:26.668
Dad never spoke about it again.

00:29:26.701 --> 00:29:29.701
I didn't ask.

00:29:29.734 --> 00:29:32.234
But he, uh...

00:29:34.401 --> 00:29:39.501
He looked at me different,
you know, which was worse.

00:29:39.534 --> 00:29:41.000
Not that i blame him.

00:29:41.034 --> 00:29:43.900
He gave me an order,
and i didn't listen,

00:29:43.933 --> 00:29:46.067
And i almost got you killed.

00:29:46.100 --> 00:29:47.501
You were just a kid.

00:29:47.534 --> 00:29:51.501
Don't.

00:29:51.534 --> 00:29:56.034
Dad knew this was
unfinished business for me.

00:29:56.067 --> 00:29:59.267
He sent me here to finish it.

00:30:01.334 --> 00:30:05.134
But using michael
- I don't know, dean.

00:30:05.167 --> 00:30:08.367
I mean, how about one of
us hides under the cover?

00:30:08.401 --> 00:30:11.267
You know, we'll be the bait.

00:30:11.301 --> 00:30:14.267
No, that won't work.

00:30:14.301 --> 00:30:17.301
It's got to get close
enough to feed. It'll see us.

00:30:19.867 --> 00:30:22.367
Believe me, i don't like it,
but it's got to be the kid.

00:30:27.967 --> 00:30:29.933
Michael: you're crazy!

00:30:29.967 --> 00:30:32.567
Just go away or i'm calling the cops.

00:30:32.601 --> 00:30:34.634
Hang on a second. Just listen to me.

00:30:34.668 --> 00:30:37.134
You have to believe me, okay?

00:30:37.167 --> 00:30:38.734
This thing came through the window

00:30:38.768 --> 00:30:39.933
And attacked your brother.

00:30:42.501 --> 00:30:43.567
I've seen it.

00:30:43.601 --> 00:30:45.100
I know what it looks like

00:30:45.134 --> 00:30:47.601
'Cause it attacked my brother once, too.

00:30:54.833 --> 00:30:56.768
This thing -

00:30:56.800 --> 00:30:59.434
Is it, like...

00:30:59.467 --> 00:31:04.000
It has this long, black robe?

00:31:04.034 --> 00:31:06.267
You saw it last night, didn't you?

00:31:06.301 --> 00:31:10.267
I thought i was having a nightmare.

00:31:12.334 --> 00:31:16.301
I'd give anything not to tell you this,

00:31:16.334 --> 00:31:18.401
But sometimes nightmares are real.

00:31:18.434 --> 00:31:21.534
<i>So why are you telling me?</i>

00:31:21.567 --> 00:31:23.334
Because we need your help.

00:31:23.367 --> 00:31:24.734
My help?

00:31:24.768 --> 00:31:29.501
We can kill it, me and
him. It's what we do.

00:31:29.534 --> 00:31:31.567
But we can't do it without you.

00:31:31.601 --> 00:31:34.800
What? No.

00:31:34.833 --> 00:31:36.534
Michael, listen to me.

00:31:36.567 --> 00:31:38.301
This thing hurt asher,

00:31:38.334 --> 00:31:41.534
And it's gonna keep hurting
kids unless we stop it.

00:31:41.567 --> 00:31:43.000
Do you understand me?

00:31:45.701 --> 00:31:48.634
Well, that went crappy. Now what?

00:31:48.668 --> 00:31:49.833
What did you expect?

00:31:49.867 --> 00:31:52.434
You can't ask an adult
to do something like that,

00:31:52.467 --> 00:31:54.167
Much less a kid.

00:32:02.401 --> 00:32:05.234
If you kill it, will asher get better?

00:32:10.034 --> 00:32:13.567
Honestly, we don't know.

00:32:16.601 --> 00:32:19.501
You said you're a big brother.

00:32:19.534 --> 00:32:21.734
Yeah.

00:32:21.768 --> 00:32:23.601
You'd take care of your little brother?

00:32:23.634 --> 00:32:27.467
You'd do anything for him?

00:32:27.501 --> 00:32:29.734
Yeah, i would.

00:32:31.634 --> 00:32:35.434
Me too.

00:32:35.467 --> 00:32:36.833
I'll help.

00:32:57.970 --> 00:32:59.604
This camera has night vision on it,

00:32:59.638 --> 00:33:01.638
So we'll be able to
see you as clear as day.

00:33:01.670 --> 00:33:02.870
Are we good?

00:33:02.904 --> 00:33:04.037
Hair to the right.

00:33:04.070 --> 00:33:05.970
There, there.

00:33:06.004 --> 00:33:09.271
Michael: what do i do?

00:33:09.304 --> 00:33:12.904
Just stay under the covers.

00:33:12.937 --> 00:33:16.437
And if it shows up?

00:33:16.471 --> 00:33:18.337
Well, we'll be right in the next room.

00:33:18.371 --> 00:33:20.937
We're gonna come in with
guns, so as soon as we do,

00:33:20.970 --> 00:33:23.304
You roll off this bed
and you crawl under it.

00:33:25.371 --> 00:33:27.104
What if you shoot me?

00:33:27.137 --> 00:33:29.703
We won't shoot you. We're good shots.

00:33:31.337 --> 00:33:34.571
We're not gonna fire
until you're clear, okay?

00:33:34.604 --> 00:33:37.070
Have you heard a gunshot before?

00:33:37.104 --> 00:33:38.737
Like in the movies?

00:33:38.770 --> 00:33:42.337
It's gonna be a lot
louder than in the movies.

00:33:42.371 --> 00:33:45.970
So i want you to stay under
the bed, cover your ears,

00:33:46.004 --> 00:33:49.237
And do not come out until
we say so, you understand?

00:33:52.004 --> 00:33:54.837
Michael, are you sure
you want to do this?

00:33:54.870 --> 00:33:56.604
You don't have to. It's
okay. I won't be mad.

00:33:56.638 --> 00:33:58.638
No, i'm okay.

00:33:58.670 --> 00:34:01.471
Just don't shoot me.

00:34:01.504 --> 00:34:04.737
We're not gonna let
anything happen to you.

00:34:04.770 --> 00:34:06.070
I promise.

00:34:18.870 --> 00:34:20.237
What time is it?

00:34:22.337 --> 00:34:23.504
3:00.

00:34:25.538 --> 00:34:27.371
You sure these iron
rounds are gonna work?

00:34:29.337 --> 00:34:30.770
Consecrated iron rounds.

00:34:30.803 --> 00:34:34.437
And yeah, it's what dad used last time.

00:34:34.471 --> 00:34:37.171
Hey, dean, i'm sorry.

00:34:40.004 --> 00:34:41.070
For what?

00:34:43.703 --> 00:34:45.604
You know...

00:34:45.638 --> 00:34:48.737
I've really given you a lot of crap

00:34:48.770 --> 00:34:52.304
For always following dad's orders,

00:34:52.337 --> 00:34:55.803
But i know why you do it.

00:34:55.837 --> 00:34:57.837
Oh, god. Kill me now.

00:35:03.104 --> 00:35:04.171
Wait, look.

00:35:38.970 --> 00:35:40.604
Now? Not yet.

00:36:15.070 --> 00:36:16.604
Michael, down!

00:36:26.770 --> 00:36:28.471
Mike, you all right? Yeah.

00:36:28.504 --> 00:36:31.204
Just sit tight.

00:36:53.670 --> 00:36:54.703
Dean!

00:37:25.137 --> 00:37:27.037
Dean: hey!

00:37:30.137 --> 00:37:31.937
You okay, little brother?

00:38:04.504 --> 00:38:06.437
It's okay, michael. You can come on out.

00:38:38.977 --> 00:38:41.044
Hey, joanna, how's asher doing?

00:38:41.077 --> 00:38:43.111
Have you seen michael?
Michael: mom! Mom!

00:38:43.144 --> 00:38:44.744
Hey!

00:38:46.244 --> 00:38:47.443
How's ash?

00:38:47.477 --> 00:38:49.577
I've got some good news.
Your brother's gonna be fine.

00:38:49.610 --> 00:38:50.777
Really?

00:38:50.810 --> 00:38:52.777
Yeah, really. No one can explain it.

00:38:52.810 --> 00:38:55.644
It's, uh, it's a miracle.

00:38:55.677 --> 00:38:57.810
They're gonna keep him in
overnight for observation,

00:38:57.844 --> 00:38:59.311
But after that, he's coming home.

00:38:59.344 --> 00:39:00.378
That's great.

00:39:00.410 --> 00:39:02.911
How are all the other kids doing?

00:39:02.944 --> 00:39:04.144
Good, real good.

00:39:04.177 --> 00:39:06.244
A bunch of them should be
checking out in a few days.

00:39:06.278 --> 00:39:08.777
Dr. Travis says the ward's
gonna be like a ghost town.

00:39:08.810 --> 00:39:12.044
Dr. Travis? What about dr. Hydaker?

00:39:12.077 --> 00:39:13.144
Oh, he wasn't in today.

00:39:13.177 --> 00:39:14.877
He must have been sick or something.

00:39:14.911 --> 00:39:17.443
Yeah, yeah, must have.

00:39:17.477 --> 00:39:21.610
So did anything happen while i was gone?

00:39:21.644 --> 00:39:23.610
No, same old stuff.

00:39:23.644 --> 00:39:25.410
Okay. You can go see ash.

00:39:25.443 --> 00:39:26.944
Now? Only if you want to.

00:39:31.543 --> 00:39:32.810
I better get going

00:39:32.844 --> 00:39:35.077
Before he hot-Wires the
car and drives himself.

00:39:41.610 --> 00:39:45.311
It's too bad.

00:39:45.344 --> 00:39:47.944
No, they'll be fine.

00:39:47.977 --> 00:39:49.344
